- agent: agent-c
- branch: agent/c/m4-w5a-port-mapping
- task: TASK-069
- summary: |
    Implemented PortMapping.from_dict() + lookup helpers in
    pysdk/pyjevsim_bridge/port_mapping.py.

    Cut-1 direction inference uses the port-name prefix:
      - "out_*" -> goes into out_ports as {port_name: fom_class}
      - "in_*"  -> goes into in_ports  as {fom_class: port_name}
                   (reverse direction so subscribers can resolve the
                    inbound port from a received FOM interaction class)
      - any other prefix -> ValueError with a clear diagnostic.
        Forces explicit direction. Future revisions may consult
        coupled_model.get_ports() (see _protocol.CoupledModelProtocol).

    Lookup helpers are plain dict.get() returning None on miss; no
    KeyError surfaces to callers.

    The dataclass remains @dataclass(frozen=True) per the seeded stub
    contract; signature is unchanged. Public surface
    (pyjevsim_bridge.PortMapping) re-exports through __init__.py as
    before.
